__pycache__/

# The agent harness. CLAUDE.md describes it as reviewable -- section G.10 calls
# .agent/deploy/** the "bản gốc" of the protected files and requires changes to
# go through a reviewed PR -- but `.agent/*` alone kept every line of it out of
# git, so there was nothing for a reviewer to review and a fix to the guardrail
# could not travel past the machine it was made on.
#
# So: ignore the tree by default, then name what is source. Order matters twice
# over. A negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# which is why each directory is un-ignored by name; and the last matching
# pattern wins, which is why deploy/runtime/ is re-excluded below rather than
# above.
.agent/*
!.agent/ARCHITECTURE.md
!.agent/HARNESS.yaml
!.agent/deploy/
!.agent/evals/
!.agent/hooks/
!.agent/mcp/
!.agent/policy/
!.agent/runtime/
!.agent/sandboxes/
!.agent/schema/
!.agent/tests/
!.agent/tools/
!.agent/workflows/

# Nothing is re-excluded under deploy/. It looks like it should be -- there is a
# .agent/deploy/runtime/ and the name reads like session state -- but it holds
# the patched policy engine an operator is meant to copy over the live one, and
# smoke_guardrail's Y1-Y11 stay RED until they do. That is the single file in
# this repository most in need of a reviewer, and __pycache__/ above already
# keeps the compiled bytecode beside it out.
#
# What stays ignored is what `.agent/*` above already covers and no negation
# names: memory/ and telemetry/ (state and counters, rewritten every run) and
# vendor/ (140 third-party files, a separate decision).

.claude/
.githooks/
settings.json

# Bộ giải mã Draco, chép từ node_modules/three bằng `pnpm draco`
public/draco/
